1445 0 obj
  << /ActualText (CPR \055 cardiopulmonary resuscitation\073 ECLS \055 extracorporeal life support\073 IV \055 intravenous\073 ROSC \055 return of spontaneous circulation\073 SBP \055 systolic blood pressure\073 C Decapitation\073 truncal transection\073 whole body decomposed or whole body frozen solid \050chest wall not compressible\051\073 G Systolic blood pressure \074 90 mmHg is a reasonable prehospital estimate of cardiocirculatory instability\054 but for in\055hospital decisions\054 the minimum sufficient circulation for a deeply hypothermic patient \050e\056g\056\054 \07428\260C\051 has not been defined\073 \234 Swiss staging of accidental hypothermia\073 H Direct transport to an ECLS centre is recommended in an arrested hypothermic patient\056 In remote areas\054 transport decisions should balance the risk of increased transport time with the potential benefit of treatment in an extracorporeal life support centre\056 Transfer should commence if such a centre can be reached within 6 hours\073 I Warm environment\054 chemical\054 electrical\054 or forced air heating packs or blankets\054 and warm IV fluids \05038\05542\260C\051\056 In case of cardiac instability refractory to medical management\054 consider rewarming with extracorporeal life support\073 \240 If the decision is made to stop at an intermediate hospital to measure serum potassium\054 a hospital en route to an extracorporeal life support centre should be chosen\056 The HOPE score should not be used in children\054 consider expert consultation instead\056)
     /K [ 83 ]
     /P 1446 0 R
     /Pg 1362 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
